    <section class="content-flow" aria-label="About AIMS Research Lab">
      <figure class="visual">
        <img src="/assets/what-is-aims.jpg" alt="AIMS research areas: computer vision, multimodal and generative AI, language models and agentic AI, edge AI, human-centered AI, and trustworthy AI">
      </figure>
      <p>The Artificial Intelligence and Multimodal Systems (AIMS) Lab develops intelligent systems that can perceive, understand, reason, interact, and operate reliably. Our research brings together computer vision, multimodal AI, language models, trustworthy AI, and human-centered intelligent systems to investigate how AI can learn from diverse forms of information and use that information effectively.</p>
      <p>Modern AI systems increasingly process information from multiple sources, including images, video, text, speech, and sensor data. AIMS researchers investigate how these systems can better understand visual and multimodal information, reason with retrieved and remembered knowledge, interact effectively with users, and remain reliable under uncertainty and challenging real-world conditions. Our research spans visual recognition and segmentation, vision-language models, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), conversational memory, AI agents, robust and trustworthy AI, and human-centered AI applications.</p>
      <p>As a student in the AIMS Lab, you will have opportunities to contribute to projects across these research areas—from developing and evaluating new AI methods to applying them to real-world problems. Students gain hands-on experience in research design, experimentation, evaluation, scientific writing, and collaboration while contributing to ongoing research projects and scholarly publications.</p>
    </section>
